  "worked_solution": "First, we need to find the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x),$ which is the solution to the homogeneous equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2033}+y=0.\n$$\n\nWriting down and solving the auxiliary equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+1 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2} & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo $\\lambda =\\pm \\text{i}$, and therefore the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=P\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x+Q\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x.\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x).$\n\nThe particular solution of the inhomogeneous equation cannot be of the form $\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}\u2061x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}\u2061x$ because this is already included in the complementary function. Therefore, we assume a particular solution of the form\ny_p = x (\\alpha \\cos x + \\beta \\sin x),\n]\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{p}$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p}^{\u2032} & =(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}\u2061x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}\u2061x)+x(-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}\u2061x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}\u2061x) \\\\ {y}_{p}^{\u2033} & =2(-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}\u2061x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}\u2061x)+x(-\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}\u2061x-\\beta \\operatorname{sin}\u2061x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha $ and $\\beta ,$ we substitute the derivatives into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n2(-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}\u2061x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}\u2061x)+x(-\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}\u2061x-\\beta \\operatorname{sin}\u2061x)+x(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}\u2061x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}\u2061x)=8\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x\n$$\n\nGrouping the terms on the left-hand side gives\n\n$$\n-2\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}\u2061x+2\\beta \\operatorname{cos}\u2061x=8\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x.\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2\\beta =0\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\,\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x) \\\\ -2\\alpha =8\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\,\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x)\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =-4$ and $\\beta =0.$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=-4x\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x.\n$$\n\nThe general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nand therefore, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny={y}_{c}+{y}_{p}=P\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x+Q\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x-4x\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x.\n$$",
